    "### Baseline Model Results\n",
    "The baseline XGBoost model achieved an accuracy of approximately 74.5%, a precision of 72.9%, a recall of 79.1%, an F1-score of 75.9%, and an ROC-AUC of 81.7%.\n",
    "\n",
    "The recall value shows that the model correctly identified about 79% of the diabetic cases. The confusion matrix shows 1,464 false negatives (diabetic cases that were missed) and 2,061 false positives. The model tends to predict the positive class more often, which is more acceptable in a healthcare screening context than missing actual patients."
   ]
