    "The ROC curve rises steeply toward the top-left corner and lies well above the diagonal from (0, 0) to (1, 1), which would represent random guessing. The AUC value of 0.824 means that there is an 82.4% probability that the model assigns a higher diabetes probability to a randomly selected diabetic case than to a randomly selected non-diabetic case. This indicates a good ability to distinguish between the two classes."
