   "source": [
    "`HighBP` is by far the most important feature, with an importance of approximately 0.63, followed by `GenHlth` (0.11) and `HighChol` (0.05). `Age`, `BMI`, and `HeartDiseaseorAttack` also contributed to the predictions. These results are consistent with known medical risk factors for diabetes. However, feature importance reflects how much each feature helped the model make predictions, and it does not prove a causal relationship."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
