    "### 15. Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric | Baseline XGBoost | Tuned XGBoost |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Accuracy | 74.5% | 75.0% |\n",
    "| Precision | 72.9% | 73.1% |\n",
    "| Recall | 79.1% | 80.4% |\n",
    "| F1-score | 75.9% | 76.6% |\n",
    "| ROC-AUC | 81.7% | 82.4% |\n",
    "| Cross-Validation F1 | 75.9% | 76.5% |\n",
    "| False Negatives | 1,464 | 1,375 |\n",
    "\n",
    "The tuned XGBoost model achieved an accuracy of approximately 75.0%, a recall of 80.4%, an F1-score of 76.6%, and an ROC-AUC of 82.4%. Hyperparameter tuning improved all metrics, and the most important improvement was in recall, which reduced the number of missed diabetic cases by 89. In a healthcare screening context, this makes the tuned model more suitable, since false negatives represent patients who would not receive further testing."
   ]
  },
